{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-02 07:36:15 UTC] [Agent: Scribe] [Project: read_search_error_ux] Created agent report card: AGENT_REPORT_CARD_Scribe_unknown_20260202_0736.md | action=create; agent=ArchitectAgent; agent_id=Scribe; agent_name=Scribe; body=# Agent Report Card: ArchitectAgent  ## [2026-02-02   Stage 2 Review   read_search_error_ux]  **Grade:** 95/100 \u2705   **Stage:** 2 (Architecture)   **Project:** read_search_error_ux   **Reviewer:** ReviewAgent-ReadSearchUX-Final    ### Category Scores - Architecture Quality: 98/100 - Feasibility: 100/100 - Clarity: 95/100 - Testability: 100/100  ### Performance Summary Excellent architecture design. Provided precise specifications with exact line numbers for integration points, detailed function signatures, comprehensive error schema definition, and clear performance budget (\\<5ms). Task packages were well-scoped and implementable. Implementation followed architecture exactly with 100% spec compliance.  ### Deductions - **-5 points:** Did not specify formatter display integration as explicit task package item. Architecture defined enriched error response schema but assumed adding fields to response dict would automatically display in error box. Missing task package for updating ResponseFormatter.format_error() to render the new fields.  ### Commendations - Precise integration points (exact line numbers) - Comprehensive error schema with backwards compatibility - Clear performance budget and optimization strategy - Well-scoped task packages - Excellent testability with explicit acceptance criteria  ### Teaching Notes When designing enhancements to error responses, remember that adding data to response dicts is only half the job. The display/formatting layer also needs explicit updates. Include a task package for formatter updates with specific acceptance criteria for how new fields should be rendered.  **Verdict:** PASS (\u226593% required) ; doc=agent_report_card; doc_type=agent_card; document_type